{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Init.Data.Int.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.SigmaJGeometricCarrier"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_multiplier_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_multiplier_compat","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeShadow.lean#L69-L75","doc":"Compatibility with the geometric carrier (#3942): the `true`-point `q = i`\nis the multiplier of the order-4 automorphism at `V`, and the `false`-point is\nthe conjugate family's multiplier — the shadow assignment matches `dU = J`\neigendata at the vertices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_unique","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeShadow.lean#L57-L67","doc":"**Uniqueness (the dictionary is forced).** Any assignment `f` satisfying the\nnormalization `f i = true` and the ρ-intertwining on the pair agrees with\n`hodgeShadow` on the whole degenerate pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_intertwines","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_intertwines","kind":"theorem","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeShadow.lean#L51-L55","doc":"ρ-equivariance on the degenerate pair: parameter conjugation maps to the\nHodge swap — `hodgeShadow (conj z) = ¬ hodgeShadow z` for `z ∈ {i, −i}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_neg","kind":"theorem","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeShadow.lean#L48-L49","doc":"The conjugate point is assigned `H^{0,1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_norm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.shadow_norm","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeShadow.lean#L45-L46","doc":"Normalization: the democratic point `q = i` is assigned `H^{1,0}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.hodgeShadow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.TauRhoHodgeShadow.hodgeShadow","kind":"def","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/TauRhoHodgeShadow.lean#L41-L43","doc":"The degenerate-locus Hodge assignment: `q = i ↦ H^{1,0}` (`true`),\neverything else (in use: `q = −i`) ↦ `H^{0,1}` (`false`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}